"answer": "According to the provided summary, people should try to avoid saturated fats (such as butter, solid shortening, and lard) and trans fats. Trans fats are specifically found in foods made with or fried in partially hydrogenated oils (PHOs), including vegetable shortenings, some margarines, crackers, cookies, and snack foods [MLP-3593]."
